          alt: "The male tract — where sperm are made, stored and sent. Testis makes sperm and testosterone. Epididymis: sperm mature here and are stored. Vas deferens: the tube that is cut in a vasectomy. Glands: seminal vesicle and prostate add fluid. Urethra: shared route for urine and semen. Why the testes hang outside: sperm need a temperature a little below the body's; the scrotum is a thermostat; an undescended testis stays too warm, will not make sperm and is at risk. The prostate surrounds the urethra — the whole reason an enlarged prostate causes urinary symptoms: poor stream, hesitancy, dribbling, getting up at night, retention. Sperm take about two to three months to make, so a fever, an illness, heat or a drug affects the count seen two to three months later. In Ghana infertility is still commonly blamed on the woman alone; a male factor is involved in roughly half of couples. Investigate both partners, and start with the simpler test: semen analysis.",
